1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,600
On April 6, on the occasion of his 59th birthday, Mr. Li Lu accepted questions from Chinese value investment enthusiasts in Seattle.

2
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:12,120
The question involves how China promotes domestic demand and makes full use of modern financial markets,

3
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:20,380
The impact of the trade war and the shift in world order, China's strategic choices, China's wave of technological innovation and the impact of AI on international relations, etc.

4
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:30,680
On December 7, 2024, Mr. Li Lu gave a speech entitled "Global Value Investment and the Era" at the 10th Anniversary Salon of the Value Investment Course at Peking University Guanghua School of Management.

5
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:38,580
In his speech, he talked about the confusion of the times in both domestic and international aspects, and his thoughts on these confusions.

6
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:45,960
Mr. Li Lu’s talk on April 6 can be seen as his further reflection on the confusion of this era and how to get out of it.

7
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:52,660
In particular, his idea of unblocking the two "blocking points" of China's economy is to obtain institutional dividends through the renewal of concepts.

8
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:59,380
The important trends that will promote China's economy to enter a new round of positive cyclic development are worthy of our consideration.

9
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:03,120
If you are interested in these contents, remember to like and follow.

10
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:05,740
Two "blocking points" in China's economy

11
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:16,280
Question: In your speech on December 7 last year, you called the problems that have arisen in the Chinese economy in the past few years the confusion of the times. Do you have any further ideas on how to resolve these confusions?

12
00:01:16,280 --> 00:01:25,320
Li Lu: China’s economy must enter a positive cycle and some major blockages must be cleared in the process of developing domestic demand. Here I will give two examples.

13
00:01:25,320 --> 00:01:31,640
The first is the security system. A considerable part of China's current security system still mainly relies on individuals and families for self-protection.

14
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:39,020
There is a huge efficiency difference between personal protection methods and market-based insurance mechanisms.

15
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:46,260
An important consideration for the imperfect security system in the past was that the country was still too poor and could not afford it.

16
00:01:46,260 --> 00:01:53,420
I feel that the welfare state only builds a security system when it has a lot of resources or is already very wealthy. And China is still a developing country.

17
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:57,480
The government is worried that once the security system is established, it will become a bottomless pit.

18
00:01:57,480 --> 00:02:03,260
Moreover, traditional thinking believes that frugality is good, and one should work hard and not be lazy.

19
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:07,020
But protection needs are the basic safety needs of human nature.

20
00:02:07,020 --> 00:02:13,800
If the government does not provide it, it does not mean that the demand does not exist. People are just inefficiently protecting themselves as a family unit.

21
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:20,080
For example, when facing a serious illness treatment fee of 1 million, an individual must actually save 1 million in cash.

22
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:26,760
Commercial insurance, through risk sharing, may only require an annual premium of 10,000 or less to obtain the same protection.

23
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:34,220
Another example is fire insurance. In order to protect against a fire risk of RMB 1 million, each family needs to actually save RMB 1 million.

24
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:38,420
Moreover, this money has been idle for a long time and is inefficient.

25
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:43,180
If the commercial insurance mechanism is adopted, each person only needs to pay a few thousand yuan per year.

26
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:50,140
Collect everyone’s premiums to establish a common fund, and pay compensation to any company that suffers a fire. This is the essence of commercial insurance.

27
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:55,760
It’s not that China hasn’t done anything, it’s just that the thinking, behavior and scale are not enough.

28
00:02:55,760 --> 00:03:02,740
A considerable part of the population has not been included in such a comprehensive people's security based on market mechanisms.

29
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:05,480
Concept is the key blocking point here.

30
00:03:05,480 --> 00:03:10,840
In the past, it was not that people should not be protected, but that it was a welfare.

31
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:18,920
So actually we have to solve the conceptual problem. Current methods of personal protection are highly inefficient and significantly hinder spending power.

32
00:03:18,920 --> 00:03:23,120
Insufficient protection is a phenomenon, a result, not a cause.

33
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:31,240
So I call it a blocked point, which means that it is possible to unblock it. Once adapted, huge consumption potential can be unleashed.

34
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:36,780
When we think about the issue of universal protection in the form of commercial insurance, we can leverage a lot of idle funds at a lower cost.

35
00:03:36,780 --> 00:03:41,280
Release it into the circulation of consumption and commerce.

36
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:46,240
In a market economy, the more exchanges occur, the more efficiency is produced.

37
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:49,700
A market economy is free exchange under competition.

38
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:55,740
Free exchange means that if I spend a dollar to buy something, I think it's worth it, and if you sell it to me, you also think it's worth it.

39
00:03:55,740 --> 00:04:01,980
That's the gist. When exchanged freely, both parties to the transaction feel that they have made a profit, a win-win situation.

40
00:04:01,980 --> 00:04:10,340
Moreover, the more exchanges and circulation are carried out under the market mechanism, the more money will be earned, the higher the efficiency, and the GDP will continue to grow.

41
00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:18,160
Therefore, after the blockages in this cycle are cleared, the efficiency of the economy itself, GDP, and the market will all increase greatly.

42
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:23,940
China's current savings rate is very high, but it has not been converted into consumption and GDP has not fully grown.

43
00:04:23,940 --> 00:04:31,180
One of the important reasons is that it does not use market mechanisms to solve the security problem.

44
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:35,320
There are still many people who still rely on personal family savings in the primitive agricultural society era for protection.

45
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:39,460
It is not enough to talk about security in terms of welfare and cannot solve the fundamental problem.

46
00:04:39,460 --> 00:04:44,540
In the past, the core concern was whether the country was developed enough to do this.

47
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:49,180
But changing this concept and clearing the blockages are actually not that difficult.

48
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:57,400
Through market mechanisms, all people pay premiums and all people receive protection. If the efficiency of security can be improved, everyone in the whole society will be proud.

49
00:04:57,400 --> 00:05:02,300
Historical protection of the past can be initiated by appropriately allocating some state-owned assets.

50
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:08,820
As long as there are some changes in concepts, this matter can be done quickly and great results can be accumulated.

51
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:15,360
This is reform. Even slight changes in some key systems will release institutional dividends.

52
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:21,120
The second sticking point of insufficient consumption is that the capital market does not play the role it should play.

53
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:27,240
Only when sufficient consumption is transformed into wealth will more consumption be recycled.

54
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:32,840
In a market economy, consumption can be converted into corporate profits.

55
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:38,400
And corporate profits can be turned into shareholders' gains. Shareholders' earnings can in turn be converted into wealth invested by consumers.

56
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:40,940
Consumers’ wealth allows them to consume more.

57
00:05:40,940 --> 00:05:50,020
Such a cycle is the cycle from consumption to wealth. The capital market organically combines consumption, products and services, entrepreneurship and innovation.

58
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:53,400
One side of the tie connects consumption, savings and investment.

59
00:05:53,400 --> 00:06:03,140
The other side connects products and services, enterprises, innovation, market value and wealth. When both sides are connected, the entire market economy comes alive.

60
00:06:03,140 --> 00:06:11,540
There are huge congestion points in China's capital market now. Therefore, large-scale savings cannot be turned into residents' wealth through consumption.

61
00:06:11,540 --> 00:06:17,860
At present, the external demand market turns China's production into other people's consumption, and then turns it back into China's savings.

62
00:06:17,860 --> 00:06:22,120
It was profitable for the external market, but it was blocked when it came to the internal market.

63
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:32,540
The result is that China's savings account for a very high proportion of total income. In the past three or four years, it has basically risen linearly, from 40% to 50%.

64
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:42,560
On the other hand, the proportion of personal consumption in GDP once rose to 48% to 49%, and government-led consumption may be around 55%.

65
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:49,300
This proportion has been declining in the past few years, reaching a low point last year, heading towards 40%.

66
00:06:49,300 --> 00:06:56,660
In developed economies, general consumption accounts for 70-80%, and the proportion of government-led consumption is also small.

67
00:06:56,660 --> 00:07:01,360
If these two key blocking points are cleared, the volume released will be huge.

68
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:06,420
For the first blocking point, the main thing is to change the concept to release vitality.

69
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:12,180
For the second blocking point, certain institutional changes need to be carried out, which specifically include two aspects.

70
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:16,920
One aspect is the connection between mainland funds and Hong Kong capital markets.

71
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:23,160
At present, the large-scale Hong Kong Stock Connect framework has been set up and the circulation has been established, but there are still a series of blockages in the middle.

72
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:31,040
For example, mainland funds cannot invest in Hong Kong IPOs, and there are some special requirements for public funds' personal funds to invest in Hong Kong.

73
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:37,280
There is also a need to seamlessly connect mainland savings and funds with Hong Kong’s overall capital market.

74
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:39,460
The second aspect is supervision.

75
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:46,280
Although the Hong Kong market has an independent regulatory system, the China Securities Regulatory Commission currently has a relatively large amount of regulatory intervention in the Hong Kong market.

76
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:56,260
If we want mainland funds and enterprises to play a role in the Hong Kong market, we must properly handle the degree of regulatory connection between the two places. They should neither be completely separated nor overly bundled.

77
00:07:56,260 --> 00:08:02,820
Just like the string for flying a kite, the string is too thick now and the kite cannot fly high or far.

78
00:08:02,820 --> 00:08:12,240
But the core basic principle is to adhere to one country, two systems, so that two sets of supervision and two systems can run in parallel and give full play to the advantages of the Hong Kong market.

79
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:18,940
Hong Kong is a place where foreign investment gathers. Foreign investment in Hong Kong does not depend on the total amount, but on the institutional arrangements.

80
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:24,200
The existence of foreign capital actually provides a reference for equal rights.

81
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:33,140
Including the same regulatory powers, the same funding rights, and the same rights for investor protection, it is extremely important to keep the Hong Kong market at the forefront of the most effective capital markets in the world.

82
00:08:33,140 --> 00:08:43,260
If we can protect foreign capital and allow domestic capital to have equal rights with foreign capital, foreign capital will eventually lose pricing power due to size, and the pricing power will eventually return to Chinese funds.

83
00:08:43,260 --> 00:08:52,660
These institutional changes and conceptual changes can be unblocked. There is no need to spend large amounts of real money to generate reform dividends.

84
00:08:52,660 --> 00:09:09,680
As an independent market, Hong Kong has all the elements of a modern capital market, including complete systems, laws, historical traditions, dispute resolution mechanisms, credit intermediaries, and the traditional trust of international investors and the international community.

85
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:19,260
Through the Glorious Revolution in 1688, Britain acquired the modern capital market that was born in the Netherlands, and thus began the journey of Britain becoming the first modern country.

86
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:33,520
If the Netherlands and the UK are a merger of equals, China's relationship with Hong Kong is more like an acquisition. The acquisition proceeds are often not cherished enough, which is a big difference.

87
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:41,260
If Hong Kong's advantages can be truly utilized, it can serve as an important supporting tool for the re-operation of China's capital market.

88
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:54,740
The capital markets of Hong Kong and Mainland China can operate separately. This is like the early Shenzhen Special Economic Zone, which implemented a completely different system. The two systems went hand in hand, ultimately leading to a wave of reform. The principle is the same.

89
00:09:54,740 --> 00:10:01,240
Hong Kong Stock Connect is an important initiative, but it is only the beginning.

90
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:08,760
If we can make full use of the Hong Kong market system acquired through acquisitions, we can establish a modern capital market system with credit functions.

91
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:15,740
Today's actual state is still far from this goal, and the degree of understanding and attention to it is far from enough.

92
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:24,940
By deepening reforms to unblock the two blocking points, and through conceptual innovation and institutional arrangements, we can leverage huge economic growth potential with a small amount of effort.

93
00:10:24,940 --> 00:10:39,400
This is the core essence of China's reform and opening up in the past 40 years. In fact, what has changed are some policy and institutional arrangements. But doing so conforms to human nature and the logic of the market economy itself. The result is a release of tremendous power.

94
00:10:39,400 --> 00:10:50,440
Today, people say that reform has entered deep water, and there are very few places that are easier to change. They are all hard-core and feel that the dividends of the system and reform are gone, which may not be entirely true.

95
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:59,340
The so-called hard nut, I understand, is to chew hard. Hard-biting means that to have an output of 100 yuan, you have to invest 100 yuan or more.

96
00:10:59,340 --> 00:11:18,500
When it comes to social security, real money has to be on the table. We are stuck in whether we have the money and whether we should do this at this time. Talking about the possibility of introducing national security topics in Hong Kong. But what I want to emphasize is that the above two blocking points actually do not involve these issues.

97
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:31,060
The reform of the universal security system actually replaces the security of individual families with the security of market mechanisms. We are still far from the stage of welfare state protection.

98
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:40,580
What is being solved is whether the protection is there, whether it can be more effective, and whether it is comprehensive. The security system of the welfare state solves the problems of adequacy and inadequacy, as well as fair and unfair social distribution.

99
00:11:40,580 --> 00:11:51,820
Similarly, making good use of the Hong Kong capital market does not mean re-establishing such a market, but truly making good use of an existing market. These are all significant changes in the system.

100
00:11:51,820 --> 00:12:08,260
Small changes can trigger big changes. In fact, these are all issues of concept, and they are all things that are easy to do. Because these mechanisms already exist, the insurance business model already exists, and the Hong Kong market already exists. It’s just a matter of doing a little surgery on it.

101
00:12:08,260 --> 00:12:16,280
Just like in the early days of reform and opening up, the system of household quotas solved the problem of food for the Chinese people in just two years.

102
00:12:16,280 --> 00:12:35,460
We have seen that in recent years, especially since the second half of last year, the Chinese government's overall thinking on managing the economy has undergone great changes. The core is that, judging from China's current size and changes in its internal and external environment, the source of China's long-term growth can only come from domestic demand. This is a major change in concept.

103
00:12:35,460 --> 00:12:46,280
When the economy takes off, we do need external markets, foreign capital, and external management experience, and we need to catch up with existing products. But after reaching a certain size, it becomes difficult to sustain.

104
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:56,860
Today, half of the products produced in China need to be exported, which is unsustainable. However, the transformation of China's economic structure has begun, the thinking has also changed, and it has begun to accelerate.

105
00:12:56,860 --> 00:13:18,800
This round of Trump’s global tariff war will speed things up. At this time, some grasping hands are needed, and it takes a lot of effort to speed up the transformation. Consumption currently accounts for only half, and the process is not that fast. To get up quickly, we need some institutional changes such as household quotas, dual-track system, price breakthroughs, and joining the WTO.

106
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:30,240
Now that China has made this conceptual change, it can find ways to speed up the process. Some measures, such as stimulating consumption and issuing large amounts of money, are one-time.

107
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:36,780
Because there are blockages, the water is still not flowing smoothly after being put in. In addition, the water pipe is so wide, no matter how much water is filled, it still doesn't flow quickly.

108
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:43,440
The total flow rate of a system is actually determined by its narrowest point, not its widest point.

109
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:56,120
It is useless to put water according to the widest place. It is the narrowest place that determines how much water can flow. So now we need to find the narrowest places and enlarge them. We don’t need to add much water, and the water will flow naturally.

110
00:13:56,120 --> 00:14:07,180
The two points I talked about are changes in concepts and policies. Relaxing the blockage point, which is the narrowest place, will produce a better effect than water injection, and there will be no consequences.

111
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:21,480
Many other so-called hard issues are about choosing the lesser of two evils. They are all suboptimal solutions and have side effects. What I want to say is that China still has many easier-to-reform dividends because conceptual blockages have not been cleared.

112
00:14:21,480 --> 00:14:30,260
After dredging, it can be accelerated in a relatively short period of time, and the economy can quickly change from relying on a combination of external demand and domestic demand to being mainly driven by domestic demand.

113
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:33,180
Trade war and shifting world order

114
00:14:33,180 --> 00:14:37,700
Q: What will be the impact on China and the world after the United States raises tariffs?

115
00:14:37,700 --> 00:14:43,760
Li Lu: A direct consequence of the trade war is that the United States directly increases consumption taxes on all imported products.

116
00:14:43,760 --> 00:15:00,320
At the same time, the global response and countermeasures were to impose consumption taxes on all U.S. exports. Coupled with the trend of trade protection and the increase in taxes between countries, consumption taxes on global trade goods are also increasing. There will be a deflationary pressure on consumption and the overall economy.

117
00:15:00,320 --> 00:15:04,360
The secondary consequences of the trade war are changes and shifts in the world order.

118
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:16,840
In the current world structure, the three core pillars supporting the American order are ideology based on universal values, rules-based free trade and global markets, and the United States' own hard power.

119
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:24,920
Trump’s Russia-Ukraine policy and global trade war not only shook the foundation of the first two pillars, but also exposed some weaknesses in its own strength.

120
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:37,340
As far as the free trade system is concerned, the United States' global unilateral taxation has brought deep doubts to the global trading system, violated WTO rules, and made the WTO organization seem ineffective.

121
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:43,440
The rules of any organization only make sense if they have the power to ensure that they can be enforced.

122
00:15:43,440 --> 00:15:57,000
Before, the United States was willing and able to implement it, but once the United States withdrew, these important organizations became without a central anchor. The rules seemed to suddenly become less important, and the ship began to rock.

123
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:10,240
For another example, in terms of strength, the U.S. dollar and U.S. dollar assets have always been the anchor assets in the world's financial markets. But today the U.S. federal debt exceeds 100% of GDP.

124
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:21,000
In recent years, the amount has increased by 2 trillion every year, mostly in the form of short-term debt. This year alone, the amount of debt renewal and new debt required will reach 10 to 11 trillion.

125
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:27,240
A considerable part of it needs to be purchased through foreign capital. The simultaneous trade war against all countries has also reduced the willingness of foreign capital to purchase U.S. dollar assets.

126
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:38,440
There are cracks in all three pillars of world order. Although other countries have not yet regarded it as a dangerous building, they have all seen that the existing order is not reliable and are looking for a new world order.

127
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:53,420
Therefore, the changes in the world order are irreversible, and it will evolve into a new order. What the new order will be, no one knows for sure yet. But the end of the order and its transition to a new order has irrevocably begun.

128
00:16:53,420 --> 00:17:05,300
For China, as a large economy, China must first counterattack and then negotiate. Regardless of the final outcome, consumption taxes on imports and exports from both China and the United States will increase and the total volume will decrease.

129
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:15,080
A large part of the market will be unsalable, so part of it will increase domestic demand, and part of it will be wasted. This is the most direct first layer of impact.

130
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:30,220
From a longer-term perspective, this trade war may accelerate China's economy from being driven by investment and exports to being driven by domestic demand. This transformation has been underway for some time, deepening since last September, and the climate is likely to accelerate it.

131
00:17:30,220 --> 00:17:36,280
As the world's largest single market, China is fully capable of launching economic growth focused on domestic demand.

132
00:17:36,280 --> 00:17:46,380
Compared with the United States, where consumption is greater than production and spending is greater than saving, China's production is greater than consumption and savings are greater than investment. The problem is instead easier to solve.

133
00:17:46,380 --> 00:17:51,560
I mentioned earlier that China still has many reform dividends that have not been fully released.

134
00:17:51,560 --> 00:18:03,660
For example, we should use market mechanisms to improve the social security system and make good use of the Hong Kong capital market. China's massive savings can be turned into consumption. After it becomes consumption, it then enters the economic entity and is condensed into company profits.

135
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:18,240
Then turn it into personal wealth through equity holdings and continue the next round of consumption. As a result, the proportion of savings is getting smaller and smaller, wealth is getting bigger and bigger, consumption is getting bigger and bigger, and companies are getting stronger and stronger. The economy enters a positive cycle.

136
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:23,940
Establish a new type of international relations based on culture, history, geography, and commerce.

137
00:18:23,940 --> 00:18:29,220
Question: In terms of international relations, how can China overcome the confusion of this era?

138
00:18:29,220 --> 00:18:34,320
Li Lu: As the world order shifts, China will also have the opportunity to change its external environment.

139
00:18:34,320 --> 00:18:43,440
Responding in different ways will produce very different results. This is the most important period for real diplomatic thinking, strategy and tactics.

140
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:50,420
Today we talked about that China still has a lot of reform potential, and there are also such reform possibilities internationally.

141
00:18:50,420 --> 00:19:00,480
Because Trump’s actions have shaken the foundation of the original international order. At this time, China can decide what position it will occupy in the evolving world structure.

142
00:19:00,480 --> 00:20:00,880
Global tariffs and the resulting global repercussions, for example, could trigger deflationary competition around the world. The term used in China in the past few years is called involution. Involution is essentially competition under deflation. The essence of raising tariffs this time is that, whether proactively or passively, the world will increase consumption taxes at the same time, and the total global economic consumption will shrink.

143
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:06,600
Therefore, it will bring a strong deflationary force. There may be a global involution, with countries dumping each other.

144
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:12,680
This is a classic prisoner's dilemma. I figured if you do this, then I have to do the same.

145
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:22,340
国家之间也这么做，互相之间竞争的增加就是螺旋通缩。 This is the case if there is no strong external intervention.

146
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:30,220
Under deflation, the natural result of competition is that if you don't do something, someone else will. As long as someone does it, you have to follow up.

147
00:20:30,220 --> 00:20:35,760
So choice is very important at this time. China has the opportunity to occupy a favorable position in the reshaping of the international order.

148
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:41,200
For example, China may have at least several such options.

149
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:46,900
The first is a vicious cycle as countries begin to impose tariffs on each other.

150
00:20:46,900 --> 00:21:01,840
Second, on the one hand, it negotiated reciprocally with the United States and reached an agreement, although it is still very high. On the other hand, countries like the WTO, except the United States, abide by existing rules and enforce them unilaterally, even if other countries do not enforce them.

151
00:21:01,840 --> 00:21:09,060
The third is to first declare compliance with all tariff agreements, including the WTO minus the United States, plus the new agreement with the United States.

152
00:21:09,060 --> 00:21:13,760
Then, on this basis, the regional free trade that has already started will be carried out more deeply.

153
00:21:13,760 --> 00:21:28,880
For example, the most important thing is that ASEAN plus China, Japan and South Korea, 10+3, should form a free trade area based on the WTO within the region, thereby forming a trade association among East and Southeast Asian countries based on traditional culture, history, and ethical practices.

154
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:35,940
Of course, these countries are all exporting countries, so this matter must be combined with the growth of domestic demand.

155
00:21:35,940 --> 00:21:40,940
Because the growth of domestic demand is actually incremental. China can unilaterally abide by the WTO and reduce the United States.

156
00:21:40,940 --> 00:21:53,920
Counterattacks against the United States are still there, but everything else continues. At the same time, a new East Asian and Southeast Asian Alliance based on culture began to be formed.

157
00:21:53,920 --> 00:22:04,060
Although the trade volume between China and the United States has decreased, after it released domestic demand, the increase in domestic demand was much larger than the decrease in trade.

158
00:22:04,060 --> 00:22:12,180
Then share the incremental part with the region. Based on this, establish a normative organization that goes further than the WTO.

159
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:25,720
Regional economic organizations will gradually produce global radiation effects and attract European countries to join the alliance.

160
00:22:25,720 --> 00:22:47,760
In fact, the connection between China and neighboring countries in soft ties such as cultural traditions, economic arrangements, moral concepts, and behavioral styles is far deeper than institutional ties. These non-political connections are as important as political ties. It has only been relatively weakened under the original international system.

161
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:54,740
And because of the traditional historical issues between China and Japan, it is often impossible to let go.

162
00:22:54,740 --> 00:23:06,120
Therefore, it is necessary to change our thinking at this time and rebuild a regional economic system with China, Japan, South Korea and ASEAN as the core.

163
00:23:06,120 --> 00:23:12,460
This new WTO minus the United States will have great power as Europe joins.

164
00:23:12,460 --> 00:23:32,960
As the international system is transforming from unipolar to multipolar, it is necessary to gradually rebuild a new international relations architecture based on cultural ties, trade ties and commercial ties, and ultimately form a cooperation mechanism with rule enforcement capabilities.

165
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:42,480
This mechanism is different from a traditional military alliance, but a special connection that serves to safeguard common commercial interests.

166
00:23:42,480 --> 00:23:54,120
In this transformation process, China may either fall into a prisoner's dilemma, leading to a deadlock, or it may achieve a double breakthrough, freeing itself from the geopolitical nightmare that has long plagued it.

167
00:23:54,120 --> 00:24:06,780
It has also successfully built a new pole among the multiple poles with itself as the core. At this time, the criteria for division are no longer based on ideology and social governance systems, but on the basis of regional cultural identity, economic interests and free trade.

168
00:24:06,780 --> 00:24:15,640
This evolution of the pattern will bring huge external institutional dividends to China.

169
00:24:15,640 --> 00:24:23,960
The most important thing is that China can achieve its goals by choosing how to respond.

170
00:24:23,960 --> 00:24:33,180
After the new economic order is established, the risks of strangulation and supply chain disruption that everyone is concerned about may no longer be a big problem.

171
00:24:33,180 --> 00:24:35,760
Loopholes in Thucydides’ Trap

172
00:24:35,760 --> 00:24:45,440
Q: Many people think that the problems between China and the United States are Thucydides Trap. There must be a battle between the boss and the second child, and they must fight. How do you understand this question?

173
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:55,100
Li Lu: Before the emergence of modern nuclear weapons, indeed the history of the West was this narrative. But after the advent of nuclear weapons, the situation has changed a lot.

174
00:24:55,100 --> 00:25:05,240
After the rise of China, great changes have also taken place. Because Chinese civilization and Western civilization developed independently, they have different ways of thinking. China doesn't think like this.

175
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:13,240
Even in today's world, China really does not want to take the initiative to fight the United States and strive to become the world's leader.

176
00:25:13,240 --> 00:26:02,180
In the era of nuclear weapons, the two major nuclear-weapon states and the two major economies cannot fight. This has become a basic consensus during the Cold War era. At the height of the Cold War, the two sides could only divide and conquer, using proxies in the middle. But the boundaries are still very clear and there is no direct contact. The emergence of nuclear weapons and the establishment of different economic systems have made peaceful coexistence between China and the United States not an option, but a state of existence.

177
00:26:02,180 --> 00:26:08,820
We can only exist under this prerequisite. No matter what the means, there can only be peace and coexistence.

178
00:26:08,820 --> 00:26:28,420
One cannot destroy the other. China already has the capability of a second wave of strikes, which means that if China is eliminated, the United States will be gone as well. Basically no one can survive the subsequent nuclear winter.

179
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:48,340
In this case, if the two economies do not use nuclear weapons and only use conventional weapons, they can fight for a long, long time, and the consumption will be endless and endless. AI can give the United States or China an advantage, but still not in the face of nuclear weapons.

180
00:26:48,340 --> 00:27:01,840
For example, if AI really allows the United States to strategically overwhelm its opponent, killing millions of people in China, then China will have no choice but to maintain the legitimacy of the regime and can only use tactical nuclear weapons, and the United States will also use tactical nuclear weapons.

181
00:27:01,840 --> 00:27:11,820
Then it can be developed into strategic nuclear weapons, which can attack tens of millions or hundreds of millions of people at a time, and it will be over in one or two rounds. One attack, two waves of counterattacks, and then a nuclear winter. In the end, everyone was gone.

182
00:27:11,820 --> 00:27:14,480
This is the situation today.

183
00:27:14,480 --> 00:27:24,200
Thucydides’ Trap is an inertial thinking in Western history. Use this to think about relationships today, and there are two holes in them.

184
00:27:24,200 --> 00:27:30,220
The first is that he failed to take into account China’s very unique thinking and the practices that run through it.

185
00:27:30,220 --> 00:28:11,260
China began to establish civilization in the Yellow River and Yangtze River basins. Since the Xia, Shang and Zhou dynasties, there have been constant conflicts between agricultural civilization and the nomadic civilization in the north. This process lasted for thousands of years. The relationship between China's Han civilization and the northern nomads is formed by China's traditional diplomatic thoughts, policies, and ways of thinking. China also adopted various response policies during this period, such as defense and the construction of the Great Wall for this purpose. Marriage, trade, cultural integration and sinicization.

186
00:28:11,260 --> 00:28:30,220
Emperor Wu of the Han Dynasty briefly used the decisive battle method. He worked hard and used the whole country to kill the Huns, and almost all of them rushed to Europe. But it also bankrupted the entire country and caused heavy casualties.

187
00:28:30,220 --> 00:28:55,740
After the decisive battle, the Han people were moved there. The Han people were unable and unwilling to live there. With the introduction of nomads, new ethnic groups began to rise in the north. Soon new ethnic groups emerged one after another. Because that area is suitable for a nomadic lifestyle.

188
00:28:55,740 --> 00:29:13,240
The Han could not end the conflict by fighting to the death. Therefore, the Chinese finally discovered that long-term competition and coexistence between Han Chinese and nomads was a state of existence and was not an option. Therefore, we can only adopt the methods of defense, fraternity, trade, and cultural integration.

189
00:29:13,240 --> 00:29:22,860
In fact, it means accepting this state of existence. The Chinese have struggled with these issues for thousands of years, and eventually adopted a different way of thinking.

190
00:29:22,860 --> 00:29:34,420
So China actually has the same attitude towards the United States and Europe. China cannot change the long-term existence of the United States and the West. It cannot change his values and social governance methods.

191
00:29:34,420 --> 00:29:37,740
In turn, it is difficult for the United States and the West to change China.

192
00:29:37,740 --> 00:29:56,380
So, accept this state of affairs. Chinese thinking is really different, and it is indeed not the Thucydides Trap. China accepts long-term coexistence with the United States and the West as a state of existence, not a choice. No one can eliminate anyone.

193
00:29:56,380 --> 00:30:10,240
Everyone is still here decades later, and peace is better than war. If the Taiwan issue is properly resolved, China and the United States will not end up at war. Their respective advantages and disadvantages make long-term cooperation between China and the United States beneficial to both parties. Of course this is not the dominant narrative today.

194
00:30:10,240 --> 00:30:16,740
There is actually a second loophole in Thucydides’ Trap. The cases he studies all took place before modern international society was fully formed.

195
00:30:16,740 --> 00:30:31,240
At that time, the economy generally fluctuated within a range. From the bottom to the top and back to the bottom again. The peaks are similar, not high, and there is no continuous and progressive growth.

196
00:30:31,240 --> 00:31:00,120
Because there is always a Malthusian trap in pre-modern society. Facing the problem of territorial expansion and population increase. War, plague, and massacres led to population decline. The success of some people always comes at the expense of the failure of others. As a large empire, China's population may decrease by 50% or more when dynasties change, and then start over again.

197
00:31:00,120 --> 00:31:12,180
The Mediterranean and northern Europe due to geographical reasons. It was difficult to form a large empire after Rome. It is difficult to truly break through the boundaries between countries.

198
00:31:12,180 --> 00:31:26,620
If you have been to Switzerland, you will be particularly aware of this. Steep mountains divide the land into small areas. There are four different languages. Their cultures, languages, and customs are all very different, and it is neither possible nor worthwhile to unify them.

199
00:31:26,620 --> 00:31:30,220
The same is true for Europe in a broad sense. Switzerland is even more extreme.

200
00:31:30,220 --> 00:31:42,340
Therefore, in a place like this, who is the boss and who is the second child is very important. When the population must be reduced, whose population will be limited?

201
00:31:42,340 --> 00:31:51,240
If a nation has the opportunity to dominate other nations, it will definitely do so because there are great economic benefits to doing so.

202
00:31:51,240 --> 00:32:02,340
After arriving in modern society. The overall economy has entered a stage of sustained and progressive growth. Because the pie continues to grow, starting from the UK, territory is not that significant.

203
00:32:02,340 --> 00:32:11,360
So it's not like the Roman Empire or the Chinese Empire. Occupying land but not granting citizenship rights. As long as the economic market adopts a colonial approach.

204
00:32:11,360 --> 00:32:21,880
The United States further developed to an even more extreme level and opposed the colonial empire. It is the market that gradually replaces land. It has become a bigger factor in judging whether the economy is strong.

205
00:32:21,880 --> 00:32:28,420
But that doesn’t mean that territory is completely unimportant. But it has become less important relative to the market.

206
00:32:28,420 --> 00:32:48,000
So the relationship between the boss and the second child is not a matter of life and death, but who has a better life. It doesn't have to be a life-and-death war between the two. Many conflicts can be resolved through benefit sharing. This is the modern socio-economic reality, which must be reflected in the conceptual reality.

207
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:02,800
There is some evolutionary process in the middle.

208
00:30:02,800 --> 00:30:09,500
Perceptions don't change quickly, so it's understandable that the narrative of Thucydides' Trap has received a wide response.

209
00:30:09,500 --> 00:30:15,500
But this narrative cannot realistically describe the relationship between China and the United States and the development of the future world.

210
00:30:15,500 --> 00:30:18,200
An era of explosive innovation.

211
00:30:18,200 --> 00:30:27,800
Q: Since this year, in the field of artificial intelligence, China has emerged with a number of technological innovation companies and talents at the forefront of the world. Will this phenomenon continue?

212
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:36,200
Li Lu: When it comes to technological development, I find that when different economies develop at a high speed, there will be a stage of innovation-intensive explosion.

213
00:30:36,200 --> 00:30:43,800
This stage usually occurs when an economy has been developing at a rapid pace for quite some time, and then generations of people emerge.

214
00:30:43,800 --> 00:30:54,200
Over the lifetime of this generation, living standards are not only getting better in practice, but also in expectations. They no longer have the basic pressure to survive, but they obviously have higher pursuits.

215
00:30:54,200 --> 00:30:59,200
This is when intense innovation occurs and success is achieved over successive generations.

216
00:30:59,200 --> 00:31:01,800
Real life is half a bottle of water.

217
00:31:01,800 --> 00:31:06,500
When the pressure to survive is high, you will only see half of the future when you look at it.

218
00:31:06,500 --> 00:31:11,500
When you are not under pressure to survive but are not particularly wealthy yet, you will look at all aspects and see both rewards and risks.

219
00:31:11,500 --> 00:31:17,200
Not only do you build relationships and find business, but you also enjoy life.

220
00:31:17,200 --> 00:31:24,200
When there is no pressure to survive and there is hope for the future, it becomes a natural assumption that life will get better.

221
00:31:24,200 --> 00:31:33,800
But the time of prosperity does not last long, and the habit of struggle is still there. At this time, people are actually in a very unique psychological stage, and there will be an intensive burst of creativity.

222
00:31:33,800 --> 00:31:41,800
All developed countries have experienced such a blowout era. All important inventions and new companies will appear intensively.

223
00:31:41,800 --> 00:31:47,000
In 1776, the industrial revolution began with the steam engine invented by Watt.

224
00:31:47,000 --> 00:31:55,500
Several more decades passed in Britain, during the 1820s and 1830s and the 1850s and 1860s, with several intensive waves of innovation.

225
00:31:55,500 --> 00:32:05,500
Twenty years after Germany was unified in 1871, from 1890 to 1910, there was an unprecedented stage of intensive innovation in science, technology, and industry.

226
00:32:05,500 --> 00:32:13,800
In the United States, one was from 1880 to 1910, 20 years after the Civil War, and the other was from 1940 to 1960 after World War II.

227
00:32:13,800 --> 00:32:20,200
Two consecutive decades of successive innovations have emerged, and a large number of people who dare to think and act have emerged.

228
00:32:20,200 --> 00:32:27,800
The special thing about the United States is that in addition to local talents, it also attracts a large number of talents from other countries, arriving in waves.

229
00:32:27,800 --> 00:32:34,800
In one wave, a spurt of innovation will generally begin in the second generation. It is really different from other countries.

230
00:32:34,800 --> 00:32:41,500
In fact, this is still the case today, and innovations in areas such as the Internet, cloud computing, and AI are still ongoing.

231
00:32:41,500 --> 00:32:44,800
China may have begun to enter such a period.

232
00:32:44,800 --> 00:32:54,500
The foundation for the industrial revolution was already there, and the infrastructure was complete. A new generation of young people has emerged who are well-educated and are not forced by the pressure of basic survival.

233
00:32:54,500 --> 00:33:04,500
This group of people is basically concentrated between the ages of 20 and 40, around 30 years old. Throughout their lives, each year is a little better than before, with few setbacks.

234
00:33:04,500 --> 00:33:11,500
They understand the world better, are more confident about the future, and hope to live, create and think in different ways.

235
00:33:11,500 --> 00:33:24,200
Generations of people in China are moving in this direction. This round of reform dividends is superficially caused by the system, but at its core is actually the change of the times. Behind it is human nature and changes in people.

236
00:33:24,200 --> 00:33:33,500
There will be outstanding entrepreneurs in every generation. The Ren Zhengfei era produced a unique Ren Zhengfei, and the Wang Chuanfu era also produced a group of remarkable entrepreneurs.

237
00:33:33,500 --> 00:33:39,500
When you get to the next generation, you will find that innovation is becoming more and more intensive, and it is not so painful.

238
00:33:39,500 --> 00:33:49,500
You will find that God is sending talents in various ways. Can see a lot of luck, see a lot of things become easier, and have an impact on each other.

239
00:33:49,500 --> 00:33:57,800
At this time, if we open up domestic consumption and open up the narrowest pipes, we may not need to pour any water, and the water will start to gush.

240
00:33:57,800 --> 00:34:05,500
The premise of everything is to relax the environment, open up the narrowest places, let the water flow, and it will naturally form a surge.

241
00:34:05,500 --> 00:34:09,800
AI development makes cooperation between countries more important.

242
00:34:09,800 --> 00:34:14,200
Q: What do you think of the impact of AI development on international relations?

243
00:34:14,200 --> 00:34:19,200
Li Lu: The fundamental challenges facing the development of AI stem from the joint action of three driving forces.

244
00:34:19,200 --> 00:34:30,200
The first is the competition law of the market economy itself. Any technology that can replace human work will naturally enter a competitive sequence, and this law continues to push technology forward.

245
00:34:30,200 --> 00:34:42,200
The second is the realistic pressure of international competition. Military technological advantages and economic competition demands have prompted countries to regard AI as a strategic area of contention, forming a national-level development thrust.

246
00:34:42,200 --> 00:34:51,200
The third is people’s permanent curiosity about knowledge itself. The instinctive pursuit of knowledge exploration constitutes the spiritual drive to break through the boundaries of technology.

247
00:34:51,200 --> 00:35:05,500
The intertwining of these three forces makes the development of AI show a single direction. Regardless of whether general intelligence (AGI) or super intelligence (ASI) can ultimately be achieved, technological evolution is always advancing in the direction of approaching and surpassing human intelligence.

248
00:35:05,500 --> 00:35:21,500
This direction is very exciting and will provide a huge boost to productivity. At the same time, it may cause short-term shock waves that are difficult to digest in employment, work, information dissemination methods, education methods, etc., and challenge the social organization methods of various countries and international relations.

249
00:35:21,500 --> 00:35:35,500
More importantly, when technology approaches the critical point of AGI and ASI, its impact will fundamentally change. The impact at this time is no longer limited to business competition or international games, but directly threatens the foundation of human existence as independent intelligence.

250
00:35:35,500 --> 00:35:43,500
This fundamental shift will create a historic turning point and force all mankind to jointly face the existential challenges brought about by technology.

251
00:35:43,500 --> 00:35:51,000
It should be noted that the current technology has not yet reached this stage, and no one can accurately predict whether it can be achieved and how likely it is.

252
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:59,800
However, the three driving forces: economic competition gains, geopolitical pressure, and curiosity drive have created irreversible inertia in technological evolution.

253
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:14,200
When this kind of challenge arises, such a challenging moment will appear as if aliens have arrived. Suddenly people discovered that new intelligence has begun to challenge human beings' status as the dominant animal on the earth in all aspects.

254
00:36:14,200 --> 00:36:22,800
Everyone will wake up. At this time, all the differences between countries, ethnic groups, cultures, histories, and rich and poor become less important.

255
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:30,200
When aliens far beyond human capabilities suddenly arrive, all responses are the same, that is, how should we survive.

256
00:36:30,200 --> 00:36:39,500
Humanity's country, race, geography, and religion are no longer important. At this time government remains the most important basic structure for organizing human response.

257
00:36:39,500 --> 00:36:44,500
Moreover, cooperation between major powers’ governments has become the only option.

258
00:36:44,500 --> 00:36:52,800
Therefore, when people keep moving forward and find that they cannot stop or stop them, their willingness to cooperate will become stronger at certain moments.

259
00:36:52,800 --> 00:37:08,200
Today, countries are still investing heavily in AI research and development. But to deal with the above risks, whether they are risks caused by strong economic and social shock waves, or more fundamental risks to human survival caused by AI turning from tools to spiritual species.

260
00:37:08,200 --> 00:37:13,800
All countries, especially major AI countries like the United States and China, need to work closely together to respond together.

261
00:37:13,800 --> 00:37:27,500
Faced with such powerful and rapidly iterating technologies, cooperation between China and the United States has increasingly become a state of survival, rather than an option. The Q&A ends here, don’t forget to like and follow.
